say CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0 turns off \"only the computed-verb and opaque-feeder forms\". It also turns off the env ambiguous-launcher form (line 357).\n- P2-5. bash_indirect_guard.py:457 treats python's -E (ignore environment) as an eval flag. python3 -E tool.py PROTOCOL.md is then blocked with a misleading \"indirect shell execution\" message.\n- P2-6. bash_indirect_telemetry.py:51-58 writes one marker file per session per switch under <audit dir>/bash-indirect-disabled/ and never prunes them.\n- P2-7. Adjacent file, reviewed in another payload: check_canonical_edit.py:616-640.\n  - If any component imported at canonical_edit/__init__.py:12 raises ImportError, every Edit/Write is blocked, canonical path or not.\n  - A non-ImportError failure, such as a SyntaxError from a truncated file, instead allows every edit, canonical paths included.\n  - ADR-202:56-59 assigns this to separate import-integrity work. The CHANGELOG should say what an adopter sees after a partial copy.\n  - In fallback mode, _cli_is_canonical is undefined, so the --is-canonical oracle raises NameError.\n- P2-8. Cosmetic issues in audit_emit.py:\n  - Lines 473-480: emit_generic has three identical branches.\n  - Lines 21 and 382-383: a pre-install iter_events delegates to the unbound template module. It is overwritten at lines 415 and 460, so it has no runtime effect.\n\nChecked and found clean\n- audit_emit facade end:\n  - 25 names removed from the facade were spot-checked, and each is exported by a part.\n  - The locks are recreated after install (lines 483-484) and are never deep-copied.\n  - _try_rate_admit's globals() resolves to the facade.\n  - _KNOWN_ACTIONS contains learning_rail_disabled.\n  - The rail and switch enums gain bash_indirect and both switch names (lifecycle_schemas.py:508-517), matching CHANGELOG lines 105-106.\n  - The spool forensic emitter is still wired.\n- Telemetry:\n  - It catches every exception, so it can never change the verdict.\n  - The marker is created