{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78DQQQ2H9Qcipyxuab6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0158xg3Mbo2TdV4uun8jeSkq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-16.verdict.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6180,"cache_read_input_tokens":129862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6180},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"447e2ee8-eb2d-46ed-af95-50cde31c949e","uuid":"f290a4b3-d8cb-47c6-9b3f-2588739dc5aa","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:02:36.949Z","request_id":"req_011Ch78DQCVumBkYnJFtreU7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0158xg3Mbo2TdV4uun8jeSkq":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-16.verdict.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0158xg3Mbo2TdV4uun8jeSkq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPayload 16: no declared condition demonstrated false; no P0 found.\n2\t\n3\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n4\t\n5\tP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:167\n6\tThe command-substitution scanner treats quoted closing parentheses as terminators. The harmless command printf '%s\\n' \"$(git log -1 --format='(%h)')\" is blocked as bash_indirect_unparseable_shell. Confirmed through decide_command; disabling heuristics does not help. Minimal fix: track quotes, escapes and nesting when locating substitution boundaries.\n7\t\n8\tP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:455\n9\tEvery canonical-path operand following an interpreter's inline program is treated as a write target. Even python3 -c 'import sys; print(sys.argv[1])' PROTOCOL.md is blocked as bash_computed_canonical_target. Read-only file inspection is also blocked. Confirmed through decide_command, including with heuristics disabled. Minimal fix: require a recognized write operation before classifying interpreter operands as write targets.\n10\t\n11\tP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:347\n12\tStatic finding: recursive xargs/find processing calls _scan_segment directly without checking MAX_DEPTH. Deep launcher nesting can exhaust Python recursion while within the input caps. The exception reaches decisions_cli.py:243–248, which emits allow: an input-limit failure becomes fail-open. Minimal fix: enforce the depth ceiling at _scan_segment entry and return bash_indirect_limit.\n13\t\n14\tP2 follow-ups\n15\t\n16\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py:53\n17\tA pre-existing symlink at bash-indirect-disabled redirects marker creation outside the audit directory. O_EXCL protects the final filename, not its parent; the resulting files are empty markers, without overwriting existing files. Minimal fix: validate and open the marker directory without following symlinks, then create markers relative to its directory descriptor.\n18\t\n19\tValidation: both false blocks disappear when only the new scanner is disabled. Python 3.9 syntax checks passed for the new scanner, telemetry and canonical binding/decisions files. Static audit/canonical binding review found no concrete regression. Audit emission was stubbed during decision probes; no files were modified. Redaction artifacts were excluded.\n20\t\n21\tVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS The findings warrant follow-up, but this payload establishes neither a false declared condition nor a P0.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"447e2ee8-eb2d-46ed-af95-50cde31c949e","uuid":"67799678-2f0c-47df-9596-431cdbff9ab8","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:02:36.969Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-16.verdict.txt","content":"Payload 16: no declared condition demonstrated false; no P0 found.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:167\nThe command-substitution scanner treats quoted closing parentheses as terminators. The harmless command printf '%s\\n' \"$(git log -1 --format='(%h)')\" is blocked as bash_indirect_unparseable_shell. Confirmed through decide_command; disabling heuristics does not help. Minimal fix: track quotes, escapes and nesting when locating substitution boundaries.\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:455\nEvery canonical-path operand following an interpreter's inline program is treated as a write target. Even python3 -c 'import sys; print(sys.argv[1])' PROTOCOL.md is blocked as bash_computed_canonical_target. Read-only file inspection is also blocked. Confirmed through decide_command, including with heuristics disabled. Minimal fix: require a recognized write operation before classifying interpreter operands as write targets.\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:347\nStatic finding: recursive xargs/find processing calls _scan_segment directly without checking MAX_DEPTH. Deep launcher nesting can exhaust Python recursion while within the input caps. The exception reaches decisions_cli.py:243–248, which emits allow: an input-limit failure becomes fail-open. Minimal fix: enforce the depth ceiling at _scan_segment entry and return bash_indirect_limit.\n\nP2 follow-ups\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py:53\nA pre-existing symlink at bash-indirect-disabled redirects marker creation outside the audit directory. O_EXCL protects the final filename, not its parent; the resulting files are empty markers, without overwriting existing files. Minimal fix: validate and open the marker directory without following symlinks, then create markers relative to its directory descriptor.\n\nValidation: both false blocks disappear when only the new scanner is disabled. Python 3.9 syntax checks passed for the new scanner, telemetry and canonical binding/decisions files. Static audit/canonical binding review found no concrete regression. Audit emission was stubbed during decision probes; no files were modified. Redaction artifacts were excluded.\n\nVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS The findings warrant follow-up, but this payload establishes neither a false declared condition nor a P0.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0158xg3Mbo2TdV4uun8jeSkq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
