rded.\n- Minimal fix:\n  - Wrap the call: try: excluded = root_claude_md_excluded(...) except Exception: excluded = True, so a value that cannot be classified becomes a TAMPER_CLAUDE_MD_EXCLUDES_ROOT finding.\n  - Make _segments_match an iterative or cached DP over indices, O(len(path) x len(pattern)), and treat a pattern over about 64 segments or with more than 8 ** as unmodelled (return True).\n  - Add a test with a 1200-** pattern next to disableAllHooks: true that expects both findings.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. Moved code broke a source-level reader: .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238 versus .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325.\n   - _sentinel_patterns() parses check_canonical_edit.py with ast, looking for _PATTERNS, which now lives in paths.py.\n   - So /ceo-boot sentinels_pending_gpg always takes its fallback: it reports \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\" and scans 4 of 10 patterns.\n   - A post-cutoff sentinel in the wave-0a, wave-0b, wave-1-2, wave-minus-1, staging/review or audit-v2 layouts that lacks its .asc is not reported.\n   - ADR-202 says source-level readers must be checked one by one; this one was missed, and no test asserts derived=True.\n   - Fix: move _PATTERNS to a module-level constant in paths.py and import it, or parse paths.py instead; add a test that asserts derived=True.\n\n2. Fail-closed on a missing component (fail-direction inversion; deliberate per ADR-202 \"AST and integrity boundaries\"): check_canonical_edit.py:616-640 is the live path; entry.py:126-133 is an unreachable copy.\n   - If any file under _lib/canonical_edit/, or _lib itself, is missing after an install or upgrade, the import raises ModuleNotFoundError. Every Edit, Write, MultiEdit and mcp__* call is then blocked, non-canonical paths included, and settings.json cannot be fixed through the harness either.\n   - This contradicts the hook's own docstring (check_canonical_edit.py:36-40, \"Any internal exception → allow\") and is not stated in CHANGELOG [1.4.4].\n   - Fix: declare it in the adopter section and update the docstring, or block only canonical-prefix paths in the fallback.\n\n3. Drift between the library and the script copy: escalation_signals.py:121-126 versus .claude/scripts/ceo-escalation-detector.py:94-97 and :373-375, which still says \"keep bit-equivalent\".\n   - The library now admits gpt-5..9, o3..o9 and claude-fable-5; the script still checks only the prefixes. No parity test catches this.\n   - The script is the stricter side, so the direction is safe, but CHANGELOG line 153 describes behavior the shipped detector does not have.\n   - The comment at escalation_signals.py:70, \"the shared predicate owns runtime policy\", is inaccurate: the legacy prefixes are still OR'd in, so claude-opus-4-1 and any claude-fable-* pass.\n\n4. effective_config.py:238: the lazy _WORKING_SET_RE stops at the first \")\", which is inside the comment at ADR-149 line 82, \"(base ... same order)\".\n   - The captured text holds no ids, so the parser falls back to scanning the whole document (:715-716).\n   - Today's result happens to equal the working set. Any quoted id added later anywhere in ADR-149 prose would silently join the allowlist.\n   - Fix: anchor the closing bracket on ^\\) (re.M), or literal_eval the code block; add a test.\n\n5. cli_currency.py:63-77: _package_files walks every ancestor up to /, and compatible_package_version (:34-51) can accept a different package.json than the one qualified_package_version (:54-60) records as installed_version.\n   - With a nested older @openai/codex package.json, or any {\"name\":\"@openai/codex\",\"version\":\"9.9.9\"} in ~ or /, the pin reads compatible/version_floor_only while PROVENANCE records a version that did not qualify. That weakens the C10 instrument identity.\n   - This stays inside the declared trust model.\n   - Fix: stop at the first package.json named @openai/codex and use that one version for both recording and comparison.\n\n6. Honesty: CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 327-328 say only a value that \"excludes the root CLAUDE.md\" is classified as tamper. claude_md_excludes.py:34-35 and :66 also flag any pattern containing { } ( ) or !.\n   - That covers brace-set monorepo patterns, negations, and absolute paths under \"Dropbox (Personal)\".\n   - Because check_config_change blocks on any settings-layer finding, such an adopter gets an advisory CONFIG-TAMPER block on every ConfigChange and a /ceo-boot finding.\n   - Separately, _root_claude_md matches only the resolved path, so a pattern written against an unresolved path (/tmp versus /private/tmp, or a symlinked checkout) is a false negative.\n   - Fix: document the over-flagging, or narrow it; match both the resolved and the absolute path.\n\n7. Doc nits:\n   - effective_config.py:35 says \"Its only shared helper\", but the module imports two (claude_md_excludes, model_currency).\n   - \"the module note above\" in paths.py (_matches_canonical_guard) and sentinels.py (_sentinel_grants_path) points at notes that stayed in check_canonical_edit.py.\n   - cli_currency.py:26 docstring says \"else None\", but the function returns -1 or 0 when the candidate is not newer, and None only on a parse failure.\n\nVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS No declared condition is false against this payload's code and no P0 was found, but one undeclared P1 (a crafted claudeMdExcludes value makes classify_tampering drop every settings-tamper finding) goes to the signed annex with a minimal fix.\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012LJcyX7ncCcwB1SXRJ7RSx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
