{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EoHkfyydCJaDBnvNQmjDEo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tNo P0 or false declared condition was established within this payload. Python 3.9.6 syntax and ordinary helper checks passed; federation package and flat imports passed. Findings below are based on static integration review.\n2\t\n3\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n4\t\n5\tP1 — .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py:624; .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/entry.py:129. Component ImportError is classified as an integrity failure and blocks even noncanonical edits after a partial installation. This inverts the required infrastructure fail-open behavior. Minimal fix: retain the diagnostic but allow on component import faults; preserve the separate fail-closed wall deadline.\n6\t\n7\tP1 — .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py:123. Failure to import guards.py silently substitutes an empty guard list. The remaining modules can bind successfully, so --is-canonical returns successful noncanonical classifications for every path. templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:243 accepts that output and never activates its conservative fallback. Minimal fix: track guard-loading failure and return nonzero from oracle mode while retaining hook infrastructure fail-open behavior.\n8\t\n9\tP2 follow-ups\n10\t\n11\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/preflight.py:52. The default policy reader still searches the facade’s top-level AST for _CANONICAL_GUARDS, now declared in canonical_edit/guards.py. Consequently, default collection raises canonical_guard_policy_unavailable and validation rejects otherwise valid packets. Minimal fix: read the extracted declaration and verify the default path without injected patterns.\n12\t\n13\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:304. Sentinel discovery still searches the facade for _PATTERNS, now in canonical_edit/paths.py. Boot therefore always uses its four-pattern fallback, omitting six supported sentinel forms from pending-signature reporting. Minimal fix: read the new authoritative location.\n14\t\n15\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/effective_config.py:544. With list-valued exclusions, a root-path resolution or glob-matching exception escapes into classify_tampering’s whole-scan handler, which returns [] and discards unrelated findings. Boot can consequently report no tamper indicators. Minimal fix: isolate this check, preserve accumulated findings, and conservatively flag exclusions the matcher cannot evaluate.\n16\t\n17\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/escalation_signals.py:126. The library now recognizes GPT/o-family VETO models, but the actual CLI retains its Claude-only predicate at .claude/scripts/ceo-escalation-detector.py:373. An admitted GPT VETO event therefore produces a false high-severity veto_non_opus incident through the CLI. Minimal fix: share the updated predicate with the standalone detector.\n18\t\n19\tVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS Two undeclared P1 regressions and four P2 follow-ups remain, without a demonstrated P0 or contradiction of a declared condition in this payload.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"447e2ee8-eb2d-46ed-af95-50cde31c949e","uuid":"6df718c4-9eea-4173-8b19-d7ebab9dfe22","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:02:43.530Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-17.verdict.txt","content":"No P0 or false declared condition was established within this payload. Python 3.9.6 syntax and ordinary helper checks passed; federation package and flat imports passed. Findings below are based on static integration review.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py:624; .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/entry.py:129. Component ImportError is classified as an integrity failure and blocks even noncanonical edits after a partial installation. This inverts the required infrastructure fail-open behavior. Minimal fix: retain the diagnostic but allow on component import faults; preserve the separate fail-closed wall deadline.\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py:123. Failure to import guards.py silently substitutes an empty guard list. The remaining modules can bind successfully, so --is-canonical returns successful noncanonical classifications for every path. templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:243 accepts that output and never activates its conservative fallback. Minimal fix: track guard-loading failure and return nonzero from oracle mode while retaining hook infrastructure fail-open behavior.\n\nP2 follow-ups\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/preflight.py:52. The default policy reader still searches the facade’s top-level AST for _CANONICAL_GUARDS, now declared in canonical_edit/guards.py. Consequently, default collection raises canonical_guard_policy_unavailable and validation rejects otherwise valid packets. Minimal fix: read the extracted declaration and verify the default path without injected patterns.\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:304. Sentinel discovery still searches the facade for _PATTERNS, now in canonical_edit/paths.py. Boot therefore always uses its four-pattern fallback, omitting six supported sentinel forms from pending-signature reporting. Minimal fix: read the new authoritative location.\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/effective_config.py:544. With list-valued exclusions, a root-path resolution or glob-matching exception escapes into classify_tampering’s whole-scan handler, which returns [] and discards unrelated findings. Boot can consequently report no tamper indicators. Minimal fix: isolate this check, preserve accumulated findings, and conservatively flag exclusions the matcher cannot evaluate.\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/escalation_signals.py:126. The library now recognizes GPT/o-family VETO models, but the actual CLI retains its Claude-only predicate at .claude/scripts/ceo-escalation-detector.py:373. An admitted GPT VETO event therefore produces a false high-severity veto_non_opus incident through the CLI. Minimal fix: share the updated predicate with the standalone detector.\n\nVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS Two undeclared P1 regressions and four P2 follow-ups remain, without a demonstrated P0 or contradiction of a declared condition in this payload.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EoHkfyydCJaDBnvNQmjDEo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
