{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012hkmo8JvYtcvJzXQqf2LDd","type":"tool_result","content":"76\tand Codex pin above. Plan an upgrade from v1.4.2 as you would plan a MINOR\n77\tone.\n78\t\n79\t### Added — a Bash guard against indirect execution, on by default (PLAN-195, ADR-201)\n80\t\n81\t- After its existing checks, `check_bash_safety.py` runs one bounded scan\n82\t  (`_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py`). The scan looks for `rm -rf`,\n83\t  `git reset --hard` or a forced `git push` reached indirectly:\n84\t  - inside `sh -c`, `eval` or a here-doc;\n85\t  - behind a known launcher;\n86\t  - through a computed command name;\n87\t  - in a program fed by a pipe, a redirect, a descriptor or a process\n88\t    substitution.\n89\t- It also blocks a computed write when it resolves the target from the\n90\t  command text to a canonical path.\n91\t- It only adds blocks; an earlier BLOCK stays BLOCK. Its reason codes are\n92\t  `bash_indirect_*` and `bash_computed_canonical_target`.\n93\t- It fails closed on a recognized shell body it cannot parse, and at its\n94\t  depth, size and word limits.\n95\t- Two switches control it. Both are on unless set to `0` in the\n96\t  environment Claude Code starts with:\n97\t  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0` turns off the scan;\n98\t  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0` turns off only the computed-verb and\n99\t    opaque-feeder forms.\n100\t- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n101\t  session and switch.\n102\t\n103\t### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n104\t\n105\t- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n106\t  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n107\t  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n108\t- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n109\t\n110\t### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n111\t\n112\t- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n113\t  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n114\t  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n115\t  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"447e2ee8-eb2d-46ed-af95-50cde31c949e","uuid":"ca816ebc-e76c-443c-9a7e-6ef61a26448f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:05:36.439Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"and Codex pin above. Plan an upgrade from v1.4.2 as you would plan a MINOR\none.\n\n### Added — a Bash guard against indirect execution, on by default (PLAN-195, ADR-201)\n\n- After its existing checks, `check_bash_safety.py` runs one bounded scan\n  (`_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py`). The scan looks for `rm -rf`,\n  `git reset --hard` or a forced `git push` reached indirectly:\n  - inside `sh -c`, `eval` or a here-doc;\n  - behind a known launcher;\n  - through a computed command name;\n  - in a program fed by a pipe, a redirect, a descriptor or a process\n    substitution.\n- It also blocks a computed write when it resolves the target from the\n  command text to a canonical path.\n- It only adds blocks; an earlier BLOCK stays BLOCK. Its reason codes are\n  `bash_indirect_*` and `bash_computed_canonical_target`.\n- It fails closed on a recognized shell body it cannot parse, and at its\n  depth, size and word limits.\n- Two switches control it. Both are on unless set to `0` in the\n  environment Claude Code starts with:\n  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0` turns off the scan;\n  - `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0` turns off only the computed-verb and\n    opaque-feeder forms.\n- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n  session and switch.\n\n### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n\n- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n\n### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n\n- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,","numLines":40,"startLine":76,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012hkmo8JvYtcvJzXQqf2LDd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
